# drivers/Kconfig
#
# SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
#
# Board/SoC-family (platform) drivers Kconfig.
#
# This directory is symlinked into the NuttX kernel driver tree as
# drivers/platform (via CONFIG_SPECIFIC_DRIVERS + BOARD_DRIVERS_DIR), so
# nuttx/drivers/Kconfig sources it unconditionally with:
#   source "$BINDIR/drivers/platform/Kconfig"
#
# Because that entry lives under the build-time link $BINDIR/drivers/platform
# (-> this directory), all our sources below use the $BINDIR/drivers/platform/
# prefix.  This matches the upstream convention used by cxd56xx and sifli.
#
# NOTE: we intentionally do NOT wrap this in `if SPECIFIC_DRIVERS`.  The
# driver-layer master switch NYABULA_CUSTOM_DRIVERS `select SPECIFIC_DRIVERS`
# (so enabling a custom driver turns on the platform channel automatically);
# wrapping here in `if SPECIFIC_DRIVERS` would make NYABULA_CUSTOM_DRIVERS
# depend on SPECIFIC_DRIVERS and, combined with that select, create a Kconfig
# dependency loop.

source "$BINDIR/drivers/platform/drivers/Kconfig"
